WEBVTT

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:47.870
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:57.940
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:08.330
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:18.330
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:28.510
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:39.030
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:49.030
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.720
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.890
"13: Tracks"

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.170
What happened here?

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.160
What does this mean?

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:31.010
We can use the plans to locate any flaws and study our findings back at the Royal Laboratory.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:33.520
Right. Good idea.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.490
Then again, doing so isn't going to be quick or easy.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.220
Oh, shoot!

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.420
What's the matter?

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.260
I'm empty! I'm all out of fuel!

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:48.530
That's all? If you're hungry,
Alicia left us something over there to eat.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.530
No, that's not what I mean.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.540
In order to maximize speed,

00:02:52.540 --> 00:03:00.080
I sacrificed fuel capacity to reduce weight in the flying vehicle we used to get here.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.750
My goodness! We're all out?

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:08.380
Oh well. We might have got here in a hurry, but we'll just have to go back with the others.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.120
Right...

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:15.220
At least we'll have plenty of time to consider why Warp Particles are decreasing.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.590
True...

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:22.570
Now that Babel is defunct, I wonder if that will have any influence on things.

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:23.970
Indeed...

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:34.270
If the Warp Particles keep diminishing at this rate, Endora itself will come crashing down...

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:43.090
Aren't those the Warp Particle measurements taken in the past?

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.490
Have you noticed something?

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.560
Well, the decrease in Warp Particles seems to begin around

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:51.230
the same time as
King Delzaine took the throne.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.430
You're right!

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:57.570
Are the dwindling Warp Particles and the king's induction somehow related or a mere coincidence?

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.440
No, everything happens for a reason.
If we can only discover the correlation...

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:04.740
The only one who knows what happened when the king took the throne...

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.300
...is the king himself.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:11.740
If only I knew what King Delzaine was after...

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.460
No one could have expected this outcome.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.360
Right. What a mess this has become...

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.130
Why? With the king dead, the revolution should be over.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.800
Not exactly.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.670
He's right.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:37.210
We can't say we succeeded, but it's true the revolution is over.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:41.370
Still, there's a mountain of other problems for us to deal with.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.650
Then again...

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:48.450
Nothing will get done on an empty stomach.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.220
Let's grab some food.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:54.060
We're low on rations so I warn you it won't be very appetizing.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.820
As long as it's edible...

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.230
C'mon. Let's go.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:16.810
There must be a way to live without killing your heart.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:18.970
Let us find it together.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.000
Emilio?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.400
Catch.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.370
You haven't even had breakfast or lunch yet.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.270
Apples are the same wherever you go.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.210
I'm saying they taste just like ours on the surface.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:56.390
Usually everything in Endora tastes like crap.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:58.050
Though I'm pretty used to it by now...

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:02.050
You... can't go back home now.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:06.400
Even though I said I'd get you back.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:10.400
In that case, I broke my promise too, you know.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.470
This is wrong!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.800
What is?

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.770
I'm not going to help your revenge!

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.480
I was wondering what you'd say.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.540
Are you too scared?

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:21.240
That's not it!

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.640
Then why?!

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.740
Just like Demetrio said, you need to talk first!

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:30.090
Come on, Emilio!

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:34.460
You... You don't understand anything about me.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.890
Emilio...

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:39.260
You're right, I don't!
I don't understand one bit!

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:43.100
But that doesn't even matter.
Revenge is never the right choice!

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:51.070
I'm not letting you go.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.470
Shut up!

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:54.640
Shun!

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.680
Emilio!

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:00.920
Ow...

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.020
You okay?!

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:02.990
Yeah.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:04.980
We've got to stop Emilio!

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:08.290
Delzaine!

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:12.690
There is still something I have yet to do.

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:17.470
Delzaine!

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.270
Emilio, enough!

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:21.440
Shun! Don't get in my way!

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.370
I'm not!

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.640
What?!

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.870
I've come to stop you.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.510
Huh?

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:31.110
I told you I won't let you have your revenge!

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:34.480
You sure did. You can't hold a promise.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.020
You deserve not to go home.

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:39.560
Hey! Don't give me that attitude!

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:42.960
Besides, you were the one who started that promise!

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:45.120
Don't tell me you forgot!

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:48.000
Listen to me.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.360
Don't boss me around!

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.330
We have to leave.

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:52.500
Leave?!

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.340
You want to go home, right?

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:56.000
Huh? Yeah...

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.870
Then I'll need your help.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.740
Doing what?

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.140
I'm taking King Delzaine down.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:03.980
Huh?! The king?!

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:07.680
I'm not helping you do that! No way!

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.380
Don't you want to get home?

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.690
Of course I do.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:13.860
But I have no intention of doing something like that.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.560
Delzaine is heading for Babylon.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.760
If he gets there before we do, you'll never be able to get back.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:20.830
Huh?!

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:24.230
That's why we have to defeat him first!

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:25.770
We have to defeat him first.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.900
How'd that work out for us? Real good, right?

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:33.610
Yeah, I know.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.070
You're right, I did say we had to defeat him.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:43.190
Back then, it's all I ever thought about.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:46.090
Revenge is all I ever lived for.

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:49.690
Ever since I was little...

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:51.350
That's all there was.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:54.460
It's such a pity, hearing that poor boy.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:57.230
He adores Delzaine not knowing he was his father's enemy.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.130
I can hardly stand to listen.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:00.600
I know...

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.700
He's far too innocent a boy.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.410
It's painful just to see.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:06.980
I don't understand...

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:08.600
What do they mean?

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:23.630
It's almost time...

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:25.890
I will end your life...

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:27.420
...with my own hands.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.600
My father's enemy...

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:45.770
Emilio?

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:57.790
Attacking someone while they sleep is proof of a coward.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.130
You...

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:05.300
You have no right to call me a coward!

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:09.170
You intend to avenge your father, the former king?

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.470
How pathetic.

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:15.310
At least die trying to seize the throne for yourself.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:18.680
Delzaine is dead.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.020
Though I wasn't the one to do it.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:26.120
It should feel like I had my revenge all the same.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:31.060
But... why? Why doesn't it?

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.790
It wasn't supposed to be like this.

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.560
In that one moment...

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:40.530
Prepare to die!

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:45.300
You're in the way, my lord!

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:54.240
Father!

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:01.580
You've become strong, Emilio.

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:25.510
I've been thinking, maybe I was wrong.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.720
Wrong?

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:31.590
Do you remember our talk on the mountain during the blizzard?

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:36.730
When I said I idolized him without knowing what he did to my father?

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:37.890
Yeah...

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:43.030
After that talk, I tried to remember my real father.

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:46.070
But... I couldn't.

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:47.800
Not at all...

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:49.540
What are you saying?

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:55.410
That final longing look Delzaine gave me... felt like I'd seen it before.

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:59.580
Maybe you remember it from when you idolized him.

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:03.120
I thought the same, but...

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:06.150
I'm not sure if I've just got it all wrong.

00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:10.890
It could be like Pascal said...

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:12.460
Hmm?

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:17.730
It was back when Pascal found out
I tried to assassinate Delzaine.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:21.100
Well, he asked me...

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:24.410
Was it really Delzaine who killed the former king?

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.770
He asked how I knew it was him.

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:33.420
I told him that's what I heard but he said that was insufficient proof.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.150
That it's just an assumption.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.650
Pascal tried to help me see.

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:44.190
Alicia worried for me too... and even Demetrio.

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:48.000
But I... I wouldn't listen to anybody.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:52.330
I could only ever think of my one end goal.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:55.170
I... I...

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.950
I wonder where those two ran off to?

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:18.160
Are you worried about them too, Falarion?

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:22.460
Don't worry. Shun is with Emilio so I'm sure he's all right.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.030
You didn't deserve it either.

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.070
Huh? Me?

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:29.970
You said it too, right?

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:33.640
That I should talk to him first and ask him the truth.

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:35.680
Yeah, I might have.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:42.720
And that even if I got my revenge, someone would be hurt by it.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.650
I said something that snobby?

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:48.920
Yeah, but I ignored every word of it.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:50.690
And this is the result.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.430
Cut it out, you're being pathetic.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:55.200
I am.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:56.100
What?

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.600
You're right. I'm pathetic.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:01.700
Quit that! It doesn't sound right coming from you!

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:05.910
Say something that pisses me off like you always do!

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.380
Huh?

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:10.950
Do you remember the huge fight we got in that one time?

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:15.950
It was right around when we joined
Demetrio and the Ignauts, right?

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.050
Yeah, it was.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:22.290
If you trust everyone that easily, you're bound to get hurt.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:25.430
You never know what their true intentions are...

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:30.130
With an attitude like that, there's no use in trusting anybody.

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:32.730
Don't you dare try to lecture me!

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:34.240
What the hell?

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:36.240
Why are you in such a bad mood?

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:39.710
Oh. Will you be lonely if I go back to the surface?

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:40.910
Don't make me laugh.

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:43.950
It'll be a load off my shoulders when you're gone.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:46.250
That is, if you ever do get home.

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:49.050
Is that any way to talk to the person helping you?

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:50.720
And to think I came along for you...

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.890
Leave. See if I care.

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:56.790
Go back to the surface and cry to your mother.

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:59.260
You really are a despicable person.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:01.560
Are all princes as smug as you?

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:03.230
You're so full of yourself!

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:05.830
That's why no one wants to help you!

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:08.000
You're nothing like Demetrio!

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.400
What do you know about me...

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:19.080
I don't want to know anything about a monster who tries to kill his parents!

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:20.480
You bastard!

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:25.520
You asked for it!

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:49.330
Son of a--

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:38.490
You kept being nasty and all I did was say one thing...

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:40.730
Just one thing?!

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:43.890
That's the one thing you shouldn't say to anybody.

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:49.240
I've never brawled with someone that much in my whole life.

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:50.540
Me either.

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:54.780
In the end, I did get saved by you though.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.210
I didn't come to help you.

00:16:57.210 --> 00:17:01.020
Back then, I thought there'd still be a use for you.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:05.950
Yeah, yeah, whatever.
It was still way too close for comfort.

00:17:10.190 --> 00:17:12.230
Hey! What happened to the prince?

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:13.360
Like I care!

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:17.390
You're a smug little shit, but I like that!

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:21.440
Dammit!

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:23.770
I don't care what happens to him!

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.210
What am I doing?!

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:30.250
I'm screwed!

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:32.270
He doesn't even matter to me!

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:47.900
Why did it have to be you?!

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:48.930
Shut up!

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:50.630
I don't want your help!

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:52.430
Just get up already!

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:55.500
Don't just stand there!

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:57.970
You always get in my way!

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.670
Let's deal with this guy first!

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:01.110
No shit!

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.850
You'll have to get past me first!

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:15.150
Oh really? I didn't know you had a death wish!

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:20.090
Shun!

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:28.000
What?!

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:39.010
His Warp Relic evolved?!

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.640
Emilio! Now!

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:49.290
I almost freaked out when I thought I was dead.

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:51.960
That guy was insanely strong.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:57.830
I've been wondering... How can you fight like that when you're from the surface?

00:18:57.830 --> 00:19:01.470
Hey now. Don't underestimate the people up there.

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:02.870
I'm not...

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:07.080
To be honest, your guess is as good as mine.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:09.240
Did you fight often on the surface?

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:12.680
Never. It's mostly a world without fighting.

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:19.220
Well, there are wars and revolts on the surface, too, but...

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:22.860
I've never had to deal with any in my life.

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:24.860
Yeah?

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:28.400
The surface... I can't even imagine.

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:29.730
Do you want to go there?

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.430
Not really.

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:35.370
But what did Delzaine want to restore Babel for?

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.670
If only I had talked to him more...

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:43.580
What are your plans now?

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.450
The same as ever. I'm still not ready to give up.

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:54.190
Babel might not be the only way back to the surface.

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:59.360
Besides, in the meantime I can meet new people and have more adventures.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:02.860
When I get back to the surface,
I'll take my story and write a sweet novel.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:03.730
Shun...

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:04.600
You really are...

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.570
Emilio? Shun!

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:10.810
Are you up there? I've been looking for you!

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:11.640
Yeah!

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:14.280
It's about time you two come back!

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:15.710
She's right.

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:25.490
All right! Let's race!

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:27.960
Quit it. You'll fall!

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:30.090
What? Are you scared?

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:32.460
I just don't want you to fall!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:33.950
Are you sure that's all?

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:37.500
Careful!

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:41.170
I'm fine!

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:43.100
That's what this rope's for!

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:46.300
Shun, you really are...

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:51.080
Finish line! Hurry on down here!

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.480
Right!

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:04.890
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:13.640
<i>I've walked very far, so far</i>

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:23.140
<i>And I'll walk even farther from here</i>

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:45.900
<i>I don't wish for everything to stay the same</i>

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:55.900
<i>Because change is what got me to where I am</i>

00:21:56.540 --> 00:22:05.090
<i>We've walked very far, so far</i>

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:13.700
<i>We'll go farther than anyone's gone before</i>

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:22.240
<i>Each of us can change the world</i>

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:31.410
<i>That's why I smile at you</i>
